        "stop_reason": {
          "kind": "finished",
          "message": "## Done — a real INI parser + printer for this repo's dialect\n\n`moon test` → **51 tests, 51 passed, 0 failed** (the 12 public fixture tests plus 39 spec-derived tests I added). `moon fmt --check` clean, `moon info` up to date, `moon check` = 0 errors.\n\n### Implementation (root package `tonyfettes/ini`, one concern per file)\n\n| file | role |\n| --- | --- |\n| [ini.mbt](D:\\a\\openseek-swe-agi\\openseek-swe-agi\\tasks\\ini_run_1\\ini.mbt) | implements the declared `parse` entry point |\n| [lines.mbt](D:\\a\\openseek-swe-agi\\openseek-swe-agi\\tasks\\ini_run_1\\lines.mbt) | LF/CRLF/CR line splitting, blank & comment predicates, blank trimming |\n| [section.mbt](D:\\a\\openseek-swe-agi\\openseek-swe-agi\\tasks\\ini_run_1\\section.mbt) | `[name]` headers, bracket/emptiness validation, wrapping-quote removal |\n| [key_value.mbt](D:\\a\\openseek-swe-agi\\openseek-swe-agi\\tasks\\ini_run_1\\key_value.mbt) | first `=`/`:` separator, key validation, carrier dispatch |\n| [values.mbt](D:\\a\\openseek-swe-agi\\openseek-swe-agi\\tasks\\ini_run_1\\values.mbt) | quoted carriers, per-carrier escape table, inline comments, backslash continuations |\n| [document.mbt](D:\\a\\openseek-swe-agi\\openseek-swe-agi\\tasks\\ini_run_1\\document.mbt) | line dispatch loop + `Builder` that assembles `Doc` |\n| [printer.mbt](D:\\a\\openseek-swe-agi\\openseek-swe-agi\\tasks\\ini_run_1\\printer.mbt) | `print`: carrier choice, escaping, section headers |\n| [errors.mbt](D:\\a\\openseek-swe-agi\\openseek-swe-agi\\tasks\\ini_run_1\\errors.mbt) | `ParseError(message, line)` with accessors |\n\n### Behaviour highlights\n- **Lines**: LF/CRLF/CR; trailing-empty final line is not invented, so `k=a\\` at EOF raises.\n- **Sections**: first `]` closes; brackets/empty/blank names rejected; only blanks or a comment may follow; one wrapping quote pair stripped (`[remote \"origin\"]` keeps its quotes).\n- **Entries**: first `=`/`:` wins, trimmed verbatim keys, control chars rejected, duplicate keys last-wins, repeated headers re-open via map lookup (never replaced).\n- **Values**: quoted values close on their own line (escape pairs hide their second char from the scan), only blanks/comment may follow; unquoted values strip an inline comment only when a blank precedes `;`/`#` (`k=a#b` stays `a#b`), then trim, then decode.\n- **Continuations**: decided on the raw text by counting trailing backslashes (odd = marker, even = literals) — reproduces the spec's N=1..4 table and keeps the blanks before the marker; continuation lines contribute text, so their `=`/`:`/quotes/comment markers stay literal.\n- **`print`**: shortest carrier that reads back unchanged (unquoted when safe, else double quotes as the exact inverse of the escape table); section names that would be trimmed or unquoted are re-wrapped, so `parse(print(doc)) == doc` holds for every document a parse can produce.\n\n### Verification\n- Public round-trip and \"never panic\" property tests pass; I added a 2000-case arbitrary-string fuzz, a 500-case fragment-soup round-trip fuzz, and exhaustive per-rule tests (escape table rows, comment rules, continuation table, CRLF, unicode/astral, git-config/systemd/php.ini samples).\n- An independent audit reproduced the parser in a scratch program and checked 3024 section-name and 820 value round-trips: **0 failures, no blockers**.\n\n### Notes\n- `moon.pkg` now puts `moonbitlang/core/test` in a `for \"test\"` import, and `moon.mod`'s `readme` points at the new [README.md](D:\\a\\openseek-swe-agi\\openseek-swe-agi\\tasks\\ini_run_1\\README.md) (overview, architecture, algorithms, usage, testing, design decisions).\n- The single remaining compiler warning (`test_unqualified_package` at `ini_pub_test.mbt:130`) originates in the protected public-test fixture, which the task forbids modifying.\n"
