        "stop_reason": {
          "kind": "finished",
          "message": "Implemented a full INI parser + printer in MoonBit for this repo's dialect. `moon test`: **47 tests, 47 passed, 0 failed** (the 12 public cases including both quickcheck properties, plus 35 edge-case tests I added); `moon check`: **0 errors**, and the only warnings come from protected scaffold files.\n\n## Implementation (root package `tonyfettes/ini`, split by responsibility)\n\n| File | Role |\n|---|---|\n| [errors.mbt](D:\\a\\openseek-swe-agi\\openseek-swe-agi\\tasks\\ini_run_2\\errors.mbt) | private `IniParseError` + `parse_error(line, message)`; every failure carries a 1-based line |\n| [scanner.mbt](D:\\a\\openseek-swe-agi\\openseek-swe-agi\\tasks\\ini_run_2\\scanner.mbt) | character classes, trimming, physical line splitting, BOM, trailing-backslash counting |\n| [value.mbt](D:\\a\\openseek-swe-agi\\openseek-swe-agi\\tasks\\ini_run_2\\value.mbt) | carriers: quoted/unquoted reading, per-carrier escape table, inline comments, continuations |\n| [section.mbt](D:\\a\\openseek-swe-agi\\openseek-swe-agi\\tasks\\ini_run_2\\section.mbt) | `[name]` headers, wrapping-quote strip, nested-bracket rejection |\n| [parser.mbt](D:\\a\\openseek-swe-agi\\openseek-swe-agi\\tasks\\ini_run_2\\parser.mbt) | `pub fn parse`: line classification and document assembly (last-wins, re-opening) |\n| [printer.mbt](D:\\a\\openseek-swe-agi\\openseek-swe-agi\\tasks\\ini_run_2\\printer.mbt) | `pub fn print`: always double-quotes values, wraps section names only when needed |\n\nKey design points: the whole scanner works on **UTF-16 code units** (all INI syntax is ASCII, so this is exact and can't split a surrogate pair); values are built **raw first, then decoded**, so continuation is decided on the raw line before escapes collapse `\\\\` (that is what makes the odd/even run-length table work); continuation lines contribute text, not syntax; inline comments require a preceding blank and are stripped from the first line only.\n\n## Verification beyond the public suite\n[ini_extra_test.mbt](D:\\a\\openseek-swe-agi\\openseek-swe-agi\\tasks\\ini_run_2\\ini_extra_test.mbt) covers the continuation table (N=1..4), the escape table per carrier, comment placement, section naming/re-opening/quoted names, duplicate keys, CRLF, unicode, BOM, view slices, real-world samples (git config, systemd unit, php.ini, desktop entry), plus a sweep of every pair of syntax characters (proving no panics) and print round-trips for awkward values/names. Test names use an `ext/` prefix and helper names are prefixed so they cannot collide with the withheld suite.\n\nI also had an independent reviewer audit against `specs/ini.md`; its findings were: `print` cannot express keys starting with `[`/`;`/`#` or names containing brackets/newlines (now documented in `print`'s doc comment and the README), one continuation-vs-comment corner (now documented and pinned by a test), and two scaffold warnings.\n\n**Important:** `moon fmt` silently rewrote two protected files (`#derive` in `ini_spec.mbt`, `Int`→`Int32` in `ini_qc.mbt`). I restored both, and verified byte-identity of every protected file (`ini_spec.mbt`, `ini_qc.mbt`, `ini_pub_test.mbt`, `specs/`, `moon.mod`, `moon.pkg`) against the pristine scaffold.\n\n[README.md](D:\\a\\openseek-swe-agi\\openseek-swe-agi\\tasks\\ini_run_2\\README.md) documents the architecture, algorithms, usage, testing and design decisions.\n"
