          "message": "The INI parser is implemented, tested, and clean. Summary of what was built and verified:\n\n```diago\ndirection: down\ninput: input text\nlines: split into physical lines\nclassify: classify first non-blank character\nblank: blank line or comment\nsection: section header, re-opens the section\nentry: key/value entry with continuations\ndoc: Doc of global entries and sections\ninput -> lines -> classify\nclassify -> blank\nclassify -> section -> doc\nclassify -> entry -> doc\n```\n\n**Implementation** (root `ini` package, one file per concern):\n\n| File | Role |\n|------|------|\n| [ini_parse.mbt](D:\\a\\openseek-swe-agi\\openseek-swe-agi\\tasks\\ini_run_3\\ini_parse.mbt) | line walk + `Doc` assembly (`pub fn parse`) |\n| [ini_lines.mbt](D:\\a\\openseek-swe-agi\\openseek-swe-agi\\tasks\\ini_run_3\\ini_lines.mbt) | LF/CRLF splitting, BOM, end-of-input rules, line numbers |\n| [ini_chars.mbt](D:\\a\\openseek-swe-agi\\openseek-swe-agi\\tasks\\ini_run_3\\ini_chars.mbt) | blank/comment/control classes, trim and range helpers |\n| [ini_section.mbt](D:\\a\\openseek-swe-agi\\openseek-swe-agi\\tasks\\ini_run_3\\ini_section.mbt) | `[name]` headers, quote stripping, distinct error reasons |\n| [ini_entry.mbt](D:\\a\\openseek-swe-agi\\openseek-swe-agi\\tasks\\ini_run_3\\ini_entry.mbt) | first `=`/`:` separator, key validation |\n| [ini_value.mbt](D:\\a\\openseek-swe-agi\\openseek-swe-agi\\tasks\\ini_run_3\\ini_value.mbt) | quoted/unquoted values, per-carrier escapes, inline comments, continuations |\n| [ini_printer.mbt](D:\\a\\openseek-swe-agi\\openseek-swe-agi\\tasks\\ini_run_3\\ini_printer.mbt) | `pub fn print`, lossless carriers, stable order |\n| [ini_error.mbt](D:\\a\\openseek-swe-agi\\openseek-swe-agi\\tasks\\ini_run_3\\ini_error.mbt) | `IniParseError { line, message }` |\n\nScanning runs on `Array[Char]` so astral characters (emoji) are never split at a UTF-16 boundary; the continuation marker is decided on the raw text before decoding, exactly as `specs/ini.md` requires.\n\n**Validation actually run**\n\n- `moon check`: 0 errors; the only 3 warnings come from given read-only files (`ini_spec.mbt`'s deprecated `derive(...)`, `moon.pkg`'s unused import, `ini_pub_test.mbt`'s implicit `Doc`).\n- `moon test`: **60/60 pass** — the 12 given public cases (incl. the 300-case round-trip and no-panic quickchecks) plus 48 added cases in [ini_parse_test.mbt](D:\\a\\openseek-swe-agi\\openseek-swe-agi\\tasks\\ini_run_3\\ini_parse_test.mbt), [ini_edge_test.mbt](D:\\a\\openseek-swe-agi\\openseek-swe-agi\\tasks\\ini_run_3\\ini_edge_test.mbt), [ini_reject_test.mbt](D:\\a\\openseek-swe-agi\\openseek-swe-agi\\tasks\\ini_run_3\\ini_reject_test.mbt) covering the escape table, the N=1..4 continuation table, inline-comment rule, section re-open/last-wins, unicode, CRLF, real-world git-config/systemd/php-ini shapes, and every rejected form.\n- `moon info`: `pkg.generated.mbti` matches the contract (`parse`, `print`, `Doc` with `Eq`/`Debug`).\n- `moon fmt`: every file I own is formatter-clean; `moon fmt --check` reports only `ini_spec.mbt`/`ini_qc.mbt`, which are shipped as-is (they are byte-identical to their originals — verified by diff against copies taken before the first format run). This and the three residual warnings are documented in [README.md](D:\\a\\openseek-swe-agi\\openseek-swe-agi\\tasks\\ini_run_3\\README.md), which covers architecture, algorithms, usage, testing, and design decisions.\n\nOne deliberate dialect decision worth flagging: a bare section name rejects `[`, `]`, `<`, `>` (so `[[nested]]` and `[<section>]` are malformed rather than names), while the quoted form `[\"a]b\"]` carries such names verbatim — the printer uses exactly that carrier, so its output always re-parses."
